Z||000003||Joe Torma||12-18-2001||03:41 PM||||Make sure your head unit has an AUX input and it will be pretty easy.<P>Are you planning on integrating the computer into the car(like me)?<P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||falconhulk||12-18-2001||03:46 PM||||I have a Pentium 166 laptop with 128 meg mem bolted to supports where the map pocket use to be.  I bought a 15 dollar FM transmitter from bestbuy I connect that to the audio out of laptop.  I also have a Garmin 12 GPS connected to serial.  I stick the small transmitter and gps on the sides of laptop with velcro.  I run AAA map and go on the laptop.  I can play CD's and MP3's through stock car stereo.  I am putting in a new head unit soon so I will be pulling this out.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Toogy||12-18-2001||04:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>Make sure your head unit has an AUX input and it will be pretty easy.<P>Are you planning on integrating the computer into the car(like me)?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't know how integrated I was planning, I was just planning on having it in the trunk with a Infrared remote running to the front somewhere and go from there.<BR>For the time being I was just going to use a tape adapter with the stock head unit until I can afford a new one<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierobear||12-18-2001||08:18 PM||||Why go through all that, unless you want to use a stock stereo? Just put in an MP3 compatible deck. I have one in my Formula, cost around $200, and it's something like 45 watts/channel.||||reg||1
