Z||000010||soup||12-19-2001||01:27 AM||||Even laptop HD's are not meant to be moved around all that much while running. To get around this all you would have to do is buy or make a supposrt with shock absorbers. Newer technology in harddrives can withstand quite a bit of shock without having the head ram into the disk. <P>I was thinking about putting a home built MP3 player in my old lebaron and the best thing that i could think of would buy an old laptop, take the motherboard and CPU out of the case and add a larger hardrive, build a custom box with good cooling, and good shock absorbers, i was thinking or a few case exhaust fans and an MDF carpeted box with a plate underneith attached to several small springs between another plate. Not so it willa ctually bounce like a slinky, but similar to what they had for CD players before antiskip technology, only larger, then run a cable up to the front where you can hook up a 10" LCD touchscreen. Run widows CE on it (operating system on palm pilots) and use that to run the mp3's. IM not sure if i can do the touch screen, and it might get to expensive so another thing i thought of was cut a hole in the consol and add a touch pad mouse, then hook that up to a basic LCD screen, Run an s-video hook up off the laptop and also run 3/4 inch stereo hook up to Stereo RCS plugged into the aux imput on my deck.. I havent really thought about putting it in my Fiero but if i did i would probably mount it on the ledge in my rear trunk. Also, if it was too awkward not having a keyboard, i would probably purchase one of those portable fold up keyboards, and have it just sit in the map pocket on the drivers side, have the chord retract into the pocket, but run through the wiring in the door back to the laptop, or use wireless like i have right now. The only real problem that I have is power. THe power supply i would probably want to run of its own battery, and i would need to hook up a 12v conector. I wouldnt want it to run off the same battery as the rest of my car, because i think that would be a pain to load and shutdown the computer everytime i want to listen to music or leave the car... I didnt read over this, and im pretty tired so some might not make sence.. if it doesnt, feel free to flame me or correct me.. : )<P>Just something i thought up while being really bored at work.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierobear||12-19-2001||01:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by voyagerspe:<BR><B>check ebay  do a search for a "aiwa mp3" you can get one in the 200.00 range ive got one in my fiero.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>We probably have the same deck. It's a piece of ****, but it plays.<P>I also have a portable walkman-style MP3 player. When I got it over a year ago, it was $200. Now you can get them for less than $100.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Joe Torma||12-19-2001||02:48 AM||||One of my customers makes that stand alone MP3 stuff... <A HREF="http://www.ssiamerica.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ssiamerica.com/</A> <P>I make their business cards btw  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||FormulaJoe||12-19-2001||10:04 AM||||Check this out:<BR> <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/ipoding/PhotoAlbum2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/ipoding/PhotoAlbum2.html</A> <P>While this is a "MAC" product (Apple actually), and you are mostly windows people, it is one option (after the windows version comes out, which is soon I hear).  The hard drive is designed to be carried around and is 5 gig.  Met a guy at a computer users meeting who had over 700 songs on his and took it everywhere with him.  Had a piece that plugged into the headphone outlet and broadcast on an unused FM frequency(he couldnt use the cassette adapter, his cassette didnt work in his car).  Even used it on his home stereo that way.  Personally for car use I would bundle the several cables in the pics together somehow to get rid of some of the clutter.  Only down side to all of this (from my point of view) is the price.  But I figure like most new devices the price will drop as production and demand increase.<P>------------------<BR>Yellow Formula<BR>(soon to be 3.4 DOHC)||||reg||6
